# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Cloudflare Pages — Dynamic Route Rewrites for Next.js Static Export
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Next.js static export creates folders like /menu/[clientId]/[orgId]/[tableId]/index.html
# but Cloudflare Pages doesn't natively map dynamic URL segments to bracket folders.
# These rewrite rules tell CF Pages to serve the correct pre-rendered HTML shell
# for any matching URL pattern. The client-side JS (Next.js router) then reads
# the actual path segments from the URL and hydrates accordingly.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# QR Code Table Ordering — /menu/:clientId/:orgId/:tableId
/menu/:clientId/:orgId/:tableId/  /menu/%5BclientId%5D/%5BorgId%5D/%5BtableId%5D/index.html  200
/menu/:clientId/:orgId/:tableId   /menu/%5BclientId%5D/%5BorgId%5D/%5BtableId%5D/index.html  200

# SPA Fallback — serve index.html for any route that doesn't match a static file
# This enables client-side routing for all other Next.js pages
/*  /index.html  200
